        "id": 1081399
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-02-09T01:41:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Consider just \"Provides\". It\u0027s cleaner.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 22,
        "startChar": 3,
        "endLine": 22,
        "endChar": 24
      },
      "revId": "606831693522173ab1bc472e4f12e80b28f28646",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6f0db68b_d8e4cf73",
        "filename": "wifi/1.0/default/hidl_callback_util.h",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 23,
      "author": {
        "id": 1081399
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-02-09T01:41:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The word \"client\" is ambiguous. And the ambiguity makes it hard to understand if this approach is a good solution.\n\nMy first interpretation of \"client\" was \"client process\". And, in that model, it seems silly to have a separate death notification for each callback that was requested by a given client.\n\nAfter reading this code, and the documentation for Binder\u0027s linkToDeath() [1], I guess \"client process\" is the wrong interpretation.\n\nPlease rephrase, to avoid the ambiguity.\n\n[1] https://developer.android.com/reference/android/os/IBinder.html#linkToDeath(android.os.IBinder.DeathRecipient, int)",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 23,
        "startChar": 38,
        "endLine": 23,
        "endChar": 45
      },
      "revId": "606831693522173ab1bc472e4f12e80b28f28646",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e491a431_bd69b157",
        "filename": "wifi/1.0/default/hidl_callback_util.h",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 35,
      "author": {
        "id": 1081399
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-02-09T01:41:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Can you tell me more about these declarations? I thought the default ctor and default dtor were implicit. (http://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/default_constructor)",
      "revId": "606831693522173ab1bc472e4f12e80b28f28646",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "060aff56_423b99d6",
        "filename": "wifi/1.0/default/hidl_callback_util.h",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 37,
      "author": {
        "id": 1081399
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-02-09T01:41:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Do we ever need to remove a callback? E.g., can a client unregister interest in events?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 37,
        "startChar": 7,
        "endLine": 37,
        "endChar": 10
      },
      "revId": "606831693522173ab1bc472e4f12e80b28f28646",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6a15dc1c_43235885",
        "filename": "wifi/1.0/default/hidl_callback_util.h",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 40,
      "author": {
        "id": 1081399
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-02-09T01:41:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is using the pointer as the cookie safe? What if |cb| is destroyed, and a new callback is allocated at the same address? Or is that the reason we always overwrite |cb_map_[cookie]|?\n\n(If the reuse concern is the reason for the unconditional overwrite, please make that explicit.)",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 40,
        "startChar": 13,
        "endLine": 40,
        "endChar": 19
      },
      "revId": "606831693522173ab1bc472e4f12e80b28f28646",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7415b2f8_cdd8c8a5",
        "filename": "wifi/1.0/default/hidl_callback_util.h",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 40,
      "author": {
        "id": 1081399
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-02-09T01:41:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Line 39 talks about an \"underlying proxy pointer\", but this looks like just the callback\u0027s pointer. Have I misunderstood? Maybe a CallbackType instance _is_ a proxy?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 40,
        "startChar": 49,
        "endLine": 40,
        "endChar": 57
      },
      "revId": "606831693522173ab1bc472e4f12e80b28f28646",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7c823067_f7acf60a",
        "filename": "wifi/1.0/default/hidl_callback_util.h",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 40,
      "author": {
        "id": 1081399
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-02-09T01:41:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Maybe uintptr_t, instead? (uint64_t is larger than necessary on 32-bit platforms.)",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 40,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 40,
        "endChar": 12
      },
      "revId": "606831693522173ab1bc472e4f12e80b28f28646",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e63a311b_12e1758e",
        "filename": "wifi/1.0/default/hidl_callback_util.h",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 45,
      "author": {
        "id": 1081399
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-02-09T01:41:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Maybe check |cb_map_.find(cookie)| before calling linkToDeath()? That would avoid a possible failure.\n\n(If we\u0027re already listening for death of this callback, no need to risk an IPC failure asking for death notification again.)",
      "revId": "606831693522173ab1bc472e4f12e80b28f28646",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
